From c6e26e2c3da7183accc82262972dd6d8418a3e28 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: LR Recomp <noreply@lr-recomp.invalid>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:59:57 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 094/108] gpu/kernel: frame-stall diagnostics (per-frame GPU
 time, upload/primitive timers, timeline observers)

- "GPU slow frame on the GPU": per-frame GPU time from the timing queries when
  over vulkan_slow_frame_ms, split by category.
- Command thread slow-frame line also times primitive processing (index
  buffers) and vertex buffer requests; render target creation logs its time.
- rex_set_event_observer (KeSetEvent, NtSetEvent, KeReleaseSemaphore,
  NtReleaseSemaphore) and rex_gpu_timeline_observer (command thread idle,
  WAIT_REG_MEM, swaps) for the game library's frame timeline recorder.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

